---
description: Architecture and coding rules for the Creeto AI prompt-to-script pipeline
alwaysApply: false
---
# Stack
- Backend: Node.js + Express + TypeScript
- Database: Supabase (PostgreSQL)
- Memory/RAG: Supermemory.ai
- Research: Perplexity API (sonar-pro)
- AI Generation: Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-20250514)
- Safety Layer 2: OpenAI Moderation API
- Job Queue: BullMQ + Redis
- Package manager: pnpm only

# Architecture Rules
- Use controller → service → repository pattern
- Controllers: handle HTTP only, try/catch on every method, call service
- Services: business logic only, call repositories and external APIs
- Repositories: all Supabase queries, never in services or controllers
- No any type. No raw LLM text stored. Zod validates every LLM response.

# Safety Enforcement
- ContentSafetyPipeline() must be awaited before EVERY Claude or OpenAI generation call
- No SCRIPT_GENERATE without FACT_CHECK status = SUCCEEDED in jobs table
- All 4 layers must pass: keyword filter → OpenAI moderation → rules engine → Claude misinformation pre-check

# API Response Shape
Always return: { success: boolean, message: string, data?: T }

# Path Aliases
Use @/ for all src imports. Never use relative paths.
@/controllers → src/controllers
@/services    → src/services
@/repositories → src/repositories
@/types       → src/types
@/utils       → src/utils
@/config      → src/config
@/validators  → src/validators
@/workers     → src/workers
@/queue       → src/queue

# LLM Prompt Rules
- Claude model: always claude-sonnet-4-20250514
- Perplexity model: always sonar-pro with return_citations: true
- Every Claude response parsed with Zod before Supabase insert
- On Zod parse failure: retry with corrective prompt (max 3 attempts)

# Supermemory Usage
- supermemory.add() after every completed script (content history)
- supermemory.search() at every generation step — replaces all RAG retrieval
- Always pass { userId, projectId } as metadata for scoped retrieval

# Supabase Real-time
- Frontend subscribes to: jobs, scripts, fact_check_results filtered by project_id
- Never poll — use Supabase real-time subscriptions

# File Naming
- Controllers: *.controller.ts
- Services: *.service.ts
- Repositories: *.repository.ts
- Routes: *.routes.ts
- Types: index.ts in types/

# Do Not
- No console.log in production code
- No raw LLM text blobs stored to Supabase
- No business logic in controllers
- No DB queries in services
- No npm or yarn — pnpm only
